            "review_title": "Review at Tonkin Bún chả - Nguyễn Công Trứ",
            "review_text": "mat_mak\nTokyo Prefecture, Japan5920 contributions\n1\nA charcoal-grilled meatball and bun restaurant popular with locals\nAug 2023\nThis small shop is located behind the hotel area in front of Marker Beach. They knead meatballs on the porch and grill them over charcoal. The tables and chairs in the shop are low, Vietnamese style. The bamboo furniture gives it a local feel. \nIf you order a bun set, you will be served a soup with round rice noodles, herbs, pickles and grilled meatballs. \nYou eat the bun by dipping it in the soup like dipping noodles. The pickles add an accent, and the meatballs have a nice charcoal aroma. The menu is written in both Vietnamese and Hangul, but there are pictures printed on the menu so you can order by pointing. Payment is cash only.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nShow original\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 20, 2023",
